md`# brain-issues

Issues of a Cloud Brain: work, bugs, feedback and security reports about the Brain and its services.

Two things are kept apart. The **record** is every event in one order, each naming the hash of the one before it and signed. The **view** is what is true now, made from the record by one function (\`issueApply\`) and made again at will (\`issue.rebuild\`).

The tracker's code is the mechanism: the chain, and the rule that an act goes ahead only when its installed guard is true. Which states an issue has, who may move it and what a move needs are a **policy**: data, installed by an event of the same record. Built 2026-10-10; the design and what it leaves out are in \`plan/cloud-brain-issues.md\`.`
// %%
viewof issuesView = issuesPanel({ client, owner: !!(session && session.owner), invalidation })
// %%
md`## Methods

| | |
|---|---|
| Worker | \`brain-x-issues\` |
| \`issue.open\` | procedure. \`{ key, title, body, kind, about, parent, labels, id }\`. \`kind\` is one the policy names (${Object.keys(issuesDefaultPolicy.kinds).map((k) => "\`" + k + "\`").join(", ")} in the default). \`about\` is \`brain\` or a Worker's name. \`id\` may be made by the caller (\`a-z 0-9 -\`, 40 at most, not \`i<number>\`); left out it is \`i<seq>\`. A subtask is an issue with a \`parent\`. |
| \`issue.comment\` | procedure. \`{ key, id, body }\` |
| \`issue.label\` | procedure. \`{ key, id, add, remove }\`, lists of names |
| \`issue.review\` | procedure. \`{ key, id, verdict, body, refs }\`. \`verdict\`: ${issuesLimits.verdicts.map((k) => "\`" + k + "\`").join(", ")} |
| \`issue.move\` | procedure. \`{ key, id, to, reason, refs }\`. \`to\` is a state. Approval and revert are moves. |
| \`issue.swap\` | procedure. \`{ key, id, swap, reason }\`: a swap the issue's workflow lists. \`{ key, id, workflow, state, reason }\`: any other, the owner present. |
| \`issue.narrow\` | procedure. \`{ key, id, move, guard, reason }\` adds a guard to one move of one issue. \`{ key, id, remove, reason }\` removes guard number \`remove\`, the owner present. |
| \`issue.install\` | procedure, the owner present. \`{ key, policy, migrate }\`. \`migrate\`: \`{ HASH: { workflow, states: { old: new } } }\` moves the open issues of workflow \`HASH\`, each with its own event. \`{ seq, hashes, moved }\` |
| \`issue.policy\` | query. \`{ policy, workflows }\` in force; \`?hash=\` one workflow, an older one too. |
| \`issue.snapshot\` | query. \`{ seq, head, policy, workflows, issues }\`: the whole view at \`seq\`. The \`body\` of a closed issue is left out. |
| \`issue.sync\` | query. \`?after=<seq>&limit=200\`. \`{ seq, wait, events }\`: the events after \`after\`, and the milliseconds the page waits before it asks again. |
| Settings | \`syncMs\` (5000): what \`issue.sync\` and \`issue.snapshot\` answer as \`wait\`. Changed with \`config.set\` on the core, no deploy. |
| \`issue.get\` | query. \`?id=\`. \`{ issue, children, events }\` |
| \`issue.list\` | query. \`?state=&kind=&about=&parent=&label=&limit=100\`. \`{ issues }\`, last changed first. |
| \`issue.verify\` | query. \`?after=<seq>\`. Checks \`seq\`, \`prev\`, \`hash\` and \`sig\` of each event after \`after\`. \`{ ok, seq, head, checked }\`, or \`{ ok: false, seq, why }\` at the first that fails. With \`guards=true\` it starts at 1 and also judges each event against the workflow in force when it was written. |
| \`issue.key\` | query, anyone. \`{ alg: "Ed25519", key }\`: the public key, a JWK. |
| \`issue.rebuild\` | procedure, the owner present. Makes the view again from the record. \`{ seq, issues }\` |
| Storage | \`sql\`: \`issues_events\` (the record), \`issues_view\`, \`issues_meta\` (the policy and every workflow by hash) |
| Secret | \`ISSUES_SIGNING_KEY\`: an Ed25519 private key as a JWK. Without it a write answers 503. |

Every write takes a \`key\`. A key is kept once: a second write with it answers the first event and \`duplicate: true\`. A write answers \`{ id, seq, event }\`. A refused act answers 403 \`Refused\` with the guard that refused it.

**Who can call**: the owner, a token and a Worker of the Brain. A member cannot yet (\`plan/cloud-brain-authority.md\` decides that).

## An event

\`\`\`
seq, key        its place in the record, and the caller's key
id, type        the issue; opened commented labelled reviewed moved swapped narrowed policy
workflow        the hash of the workflow the act was judged under
…               the act's own fields (title, body, to, reason, refs, verdict, …)
by, origin      { caller, via, holder, tab } as the core named them on this call, and the same for who started the chain
ray, at         the call's ray in Workers Logs, and the time in ms
prev            the hash of the event before it
hash            SHA-256 of the JSON of every field above, keys sorted, no whitespace
sig             Ed25519 signature of hash
\`\`\`

A changed or removed event breaks \`prev\` of each one after it. What the chain does not show: the last events removed, or a whole new record written by whoever holds the key and the database. Nothing outside the Brain holds the head (Tom, 2026-10-10: a signed chain only).`
// %%
md`## A policy

\`\`\`js
{ kinds: { bug: "task", security: "security" },
  workflows: { task: {
    states: ["open", "done"], start: "open", closed: ["done"],
    read: "true", open: "true", comment: "true", label: GUARD, review: GUARD, narrow: GUARD,
    moves: [{ name: "finish", from: "open", to: "done", guard: GUARD }],     // from: a state, a list, or "*"
    swaps: [{ name: "escalate", to: { workflow: "security", state: "open" }, guard: GUARD }] } } }
\`\`\`

A guard is one CEL expression (*Access rules* in \`@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac\`). It is true or the act is refused; an error refuses. A guard that does not parse refuses the install. A workflow is named in an event by the SHA-256 of its JSON, so an issue stays on the workflow it was opened under until a swap moves it.

| a guard reads | |
|---|---|
| \`caller.id\`, \`caller.kind\`, \`caller.via\`, \`caller.holder\`, \`caller.delegation\` | as a method's rule does |
| \`caller.actor\` | \`delegation:<id>\` for a call under a delegation (a token is one), or else \`caller.id\`. Two delegations of the owner are two actors. |
| \`caller.present\` | the owner, via \`session\`, in their own tab |
| \`issue.id\`, \`.kind\`, \`.about\`, \`.state\`, \`.labels\`, \`.parent\`, \`.opener\` | \`opener\` is an actor |
| \`issue.major\` | the issue has the label \`major\` |
| \`issue.by\` | a map: the name of a move → the actor who last made it. \`issue.by.start\` is the implementer in the default workflow. A move not made yet is an error, so the guard refuses. |
| \`issue.reviews\` | \`[{ actor, verdict }]\` since the issue came into its state |
| \`issue.children.total\`, \`.open\` | issues whose \`parent\` this is, and those not in a closed state |
| \`event.to\`, \`.reason\`, \`.refs\`, \`.refKinds\`, \`.verdict\`, \`.add\`, \`.remove\` | the act asked for |

Every fact is in the record, so \`issue.verify?guards=true\` can judge every event again.

**Fixed in the code**, whatever the policy says: a caller the \`read\` guard refuses does nothing to the issue and is answered 404; installing a policy, a swap the workflow does not list, removing a guard of an issue and \`issue.rebuild\` need the owner present. The first write into an empty record installs \`issuesDefaultPolicy\` as event 1, by this Worker. That is the one policy written without the owner, and it cannot be written again: a record with events and no policy in its view answers 503 \`ViewLost\` until \`issue.rebuild\`.

**Present is not exact yet.** A sign-in link's token made with \`unattended\` reaches a service as \`owner\` via \`session\` (\`plan/cloud-brain-authority.md\`, read 2026-10-10). Until that token has its own via, it passes \`caller.present\` unless the core sends \`x-brain-tab: 0\` for it.

## The default policy

| workflow | kinds | |
|---|---|---|
| \`task\` | \`bug\`, \`task\` | ${issuesDefaultPolicy.workflows.task.states.join(" → ")}. Listed swap \`escalate\` to \`security\` at \`triaged\`, for whoever may triage, when the issue has the label \`security\`. |
| \`security\` | \`security\` | as \`task\`, every issue needs approval, read by the owner present and its opener, no swap out |
| \`feedback\` | \`feedback\` | open → closed. Listed swap \`promote\` to \`task\`. |

Who may triage, label and narrow: the owner or a token. A reviewer and whoever passes the issue is not the implementer. \`approve\`, \`revert\` and a reject from any state are the owner present. The guards are the cell \`issuesDefaultPolicy\`.`
// %%
issues_service = cloudflare.Service("issues", issuesApp, {
  methods: Object.fromEntries(
    [["open", "procedure"], ["comment", "procedure"], ["label", "procedure"], ["review", "procedure"], ["move", "procedure"], ["swap", "procedure"], ["narrow", "procedure"], ["install", "procedure"], ["rebuild", "procedure"], ["policy", "query"], ["snapshot", "query"], ["sync", "query"], ["get", "query"], ["list", "query"], ["verify", "query"], ["key", "query"]].map(([name, type]) => [
      "com.lopecode.brain.issue." + name,
      // The owner, a token and a Worker of the Brain. A member's Worker calls as its author's DID and is not let in.
      name === "key" ? { type, who: "anyone" } : { type, allow: 'caller.kind in ["owner", "token", "worker"]' }
    ])
  )
})
// %%
issues_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", issues_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced issues_service";
}
// %%
issuesLimits = ({ body: 20000, title: 300, reason: 2000, key: 100, refs: 20, labels: 20, policy: 100000, page: 500, verdicts: ["pass", "changes", "block"] })
// %%
// The guards of a Brain that has installed no policy. Written 2026-10-10 from the state table of plan/cloud-brain-issues.md.
issuesDefaultPolicy = {
  const triage = 'caller.kind in ["owner", "token"]';
  const other = "caller.actor != issue.by.start";
  const passed = `issue.reviews.exists(r, r.verdict == "pass" && r.actor != issue.by.start) && ${other}`;
  const acts = { read: "true", open: "true", comment: "true", label: triage, review: `issue.state == "in-review" && ${other}`, narrow: triage };
  const states = ["open", "triaged", "ready", "in-progress", "in-review", "awaiting-approval", "done", "rejected", "reverted"];
  const moves = (always) => [
    { name: "triage", from: "open", to: "triaged", guard: `${triage} && event.reason != ""` },
    { name: "reject", from: ["open", "triaged"], to: "rejected", guard: `${triage} && event.reason != ""` },
    { name: "ready", from: "triaged", to: "ready", guard: `${triage} && issue.children.open == 0` },
    { name: "start", from: "ready", to: "in-progress", guard: "true" },
    { name: "submit", from: "in-progress", to: "in-review", guard: "caller.actor == issue.by.start && size(event.refs) > 0 && issue.children.open == 0" },
    ...(always ? [] : [{ name: "pass", from: "in-review", to: "done", guard: `!issue.major && ${passed}` }]),
    { name: "to-approval", from: "in-review", to: "awaiting-approval", guard: always ? passed : `issue.major && ${passed}` },
    { name: "rework", from: "in-review", to: "in-progress", guard: `issue.reviews.exists(r, r.verdict in ["changes", "block"]) && ${other}` },
    { name: "approve", from: "awaiting-approval", to: "done", guard: "caller.present" },
    { name: "revert", from: "done", to: "reverted", guard: 'caller.present && event.reason != "" && size(event.refs) > 0' },
    { name: "owner-reject", from: "*", to: "rejected", guard: 'caller.present && event.reason != ""' }
  ];
  const closed = ["done", "rejected", "reverted"];
  return {
    kinds: { bug: "task", task: "task", feedback: "feedback", security: "security" },
    workflows: {
      task: { states, start: "open", closed, ...acts, moves: moves(false), swaps: [{ name: "escalate", to: { workflow: "security", state: "triaged" }, guard: `${triage} && "security" in issue.labels` }] },
      security: { states, start: "open", closed, ...acts, read: "caller.present || caller.actor == issue.opener", moves: moves(true), swaps: [] },
      feedback: { states: ["open", "closed"], start: "open", closed: ["closed"], ...acts, moves: [{ name: "close", from: "open", to: "closed", guard: triage }], swaps: [{ name: "promote", to: { workflow: "task", state: "open" }, guard: triage }] }
    }
  };
}
// %%
issuesSchema = [
  "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS issues_events (seq INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, key TEXT NOT NULL, id TEXT, type TEXT NOT NULL, at INTEGER NOT NULL, hash TEXT NOT NULL, event TEXT NOT NULL)",
  "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS issues_events_key ON issues_events (key)",
  "CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS issues_events_id ON issues_events (id, seq)",
  "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS issues_view (id TEXT NOT NULL, state TEXT, kind TEXT, about TEXT, parent TEXT, workflow TEXT, closed INTEGER, updated INTEGER, issue TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (id)) WITHOUT ROWID",
  "CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS issues_view_parent ON issues_view (parent)",
  "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS issues_meta (k TEXT NOT NULL, v TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (k)) WITHOUT ROWID"
]
// %%
issuesSql = ({
  head: "SELECT seq, hash FROM issues_events ORDER BY seq DESC LIMIT 1",
  byKey: "SELECT event FROM issues_events WHERE key = ?1",
  insert: "INSERT INTO issues_events (seq, key, id, type, at, hash, event) VALUES (?1, ?2, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6, ?7)",
  after: "SELECT event FROM issues_events WHERE seq > ?1 ORDER BY seq LIMIT ?2",
  of: "SELECT event FROM issues_events WHERE id = ?1 ORDER BY seq",
  one: "SELECT event FROM issues_events WHERE seq = ?1",
  meta: "SELECT k, v FROM issues_meta",
  putMeta: "REPLACE INTO issues_meta (k, v) VALUES (?1, ?2)",
  // The issue, its children, and a second id (the parent of an issue being opened).
  near: "SELECT issue FROM issues_view WHERE id = ?1 OR parent = ?1 OR id = ?2",
  all: "SELECT issue FROM issues_view",
  putIssue: "REPLACE INTO issues_view (id, state, kind, about, parent, workflow, closed, updated, issue) VALUES (?1, ?2, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6, ?7, ?8, ?9)",
  onWorkflow: "SELECT issue FROM issues_view WHERE workflow = ?1 AND closed = 0",
  clearView: "DELETE FROM issues_view",
  clearMeta: "DELETE FROM issues_meta"
})
// %%
// JSON with keys sorted and no whitespace: what an event's hash and a workflow's hash are taken of.
issueCanon = {
  const canon = (v) =>
    v === null || typeof v !== "object"
      ? JSON.stringify(v ?? null)
      : Array.isArray(v)
        ? "[" + v.map(canon).join(",") + "]"
        : "{" + Object.keys(v).filter((k) => v[k] !== undefined).sort().map((k) => JSON.stringify(k) + ":" + canon(v[k])).join(",") + "}";
  return canon;
}
// %%
// An Ed25519 key from its JWK as text. With the private part (d) it signs; the public part alone checks.
issueKeys = async (text) => {
  const jwk = typeof text === "string" ? JSON.parse(text) : text, pub = { kty: jwk.kty, crv: jwk.crv, x: jwk.x };
  const b64 = (bytes) => btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(bytes))).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
  const un = (s) => Uint8Array.from(atob(String(s).replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));
  const enc = (s) => new TextEncoder().encode(s);
  const priv = jwk.d ? await crypto.subtle.importKey("jwk", { ...pub, d: jwk.d }, { name: "Ed25519" }, false, ["sign"]) : null;
  const key = await crypto.subtle.importKey("jwk", pub, { name: "Ed25519" }, false, ["verify"]);
  return {
    public: pub,
    sign: async (hash) => b64(await crypto.subtle.sign("Ed25519", priv, enc(hash))),
    verify: async (hash, sig) => crypto.subtle.verify("Ed25519", key, un(sig), enc(hash)).catch(() => false)
  };
}
// %%
issueView = () => ({ seq: 0, head: "", policy: null, workflows: {}, issues: {} })
// %%
// Who acted, as one name: the delegation a call was under, or else the caller. The holder is not it: on cb4 on
// 2026-10-10 every token's call arrived with the holder "secret", so two tokens would have been one actor.
issueActor = (by) => (by && /^delegation:/.test(by.via || "") ? by.via : (by && by.caller) || "anonymous")
// %%
// What a guard reads about who acts, from an event's `by`.
issueCaller = (by) => {
  const c = callerOf(by);
  return { id: c.id, kind: c.kind, via: (by && by.via) || "", holder: c.holder, delegation: c.delegation, actor: issueActor(by), present: c.id === "owner" && !!by && by.via === "session" && by.tab !== false };
}
// %%
// The view after one more event. No I/O: the service, issue.rebuild, issue.verify and the page all make the view with it.
issueApply = (view, e) => {
  view.seq = e.seq;
  view.head = e.hash;
  if (e.type === "policy") {
    view.policy = { seq: e.seq, kinds: e.policy.kinds, names: e.hashes };
    for (const [name, hash] of Object.entries(e.hashes)) view.workflows[hash] = e.policy.workflows[name];
    return view;
  }
  const actor = issueActor(e.by);
  const closed = (i) => (((view.workflows[i.workflow] || {}).closed || []).includes(i.state));
  if (e.type === "opened") {
    const i = { id: e.id, title: e.title, body: e.body, kind: e.kind, about: e.about, parent: e.parent || null, labels: e.labels || [], state: e.state, workflow: e.workflow, opener: actor, by: {}, reviews: [], extra: [], closed: false, comments: 0, opened_at: e.at, updated_at: e.at, seq: e.seq };
    view.issues[e.id] = { ...i, closed: closed(i) };
    return view;
  }
  const i = view.issues[e.id];
  if (!i || i.hidden) return view;
  i.updated_at = e.at;
  i.seq = e.seq;
  if (e.type === "commented") i.comments++;
  if (e.type === "labelled") i.labels = [...new Set([...i.labels.filter((l) => !(e.remove || []).includes(l)), ...(e.add || [])])];
  if (e.type === "reviewed") i.reviews.push({ actor, verdict: e.verdict });
  if (e.type === "moved") Object.assign(i, { state: e.to, by: { ...i.by, [e.move]: actor }, reviews: [] });
  if (e.type === "swapped") Object.assign(i, { workflow: e.to.workflow, state: e.to.state, reviews: [] });
  if (e.type === "narrowed") i.extra = e.remove != null ? i.extra.filter((x) => x.n !== e.remove) : [...i.extra, { n: e.seq, move: e.move, guard: e.guard }];
  i.closed = closed(i);
  return view;
}
// %%
// May this caller do this act, by the policy in the view? { allow, why }, and for a move or a swap which one.
// act: { type: open | comment | label | review | move | swap | narrow | read | policy, id, … }.
issueAllowed = (view, by, act) => {
  const caller = issueCaller(by), no = (why, missing) => ({ allow: false, why, ...(missing ? { missing: true } : {}) });
  const present = () => (caller.present ? { allow: true } : no("the owner, present"));
  // The first policy of a Brain is the default one, written by the Worker itself.
  if (act.type === "policy") return !view.seq && !view.policy && caller.id === "worker:brain-x-issues" ? { allow: true } : present();
  if (!view.policy) return no("no policy is installed");
  const facts = (i) => {
    const kids = Object.values(view.issues).filter((k) => k.parent === i.id);
    return { id: i.id, kind: i.kind, about: i.about, state: i.state, labels: i.labels, parent: i.parent || "", opener: i.opener, major: i.labels.includes("major"), by: i.by, reviews: i.reviews, children: { total: kids.length, open: kids.filter((k) => !k.closed).length } };
  };
  const refs = act.refs || [];
  const event = { type: act.type, to: typeof act.to === "string" ? act.to : "", reason: act.reason || "", refs, refKinds: refs.map((r) => r.kind), verdict: act.verdict || "", add: act.add || [], remove: Array.isArray(act.remove) ? act.remove : [] };
  const test = (guard, issue) => typeof guard === "string" && decide({ allow: guard }, { caller, issue, event }).allow;
  if (act.type === "open") {
    const hash = view.policy.names[view.policy.kinds[act.kind]], wf = view.workflows[hash];
    if (!wf) return no("no workflow for the kind " + act.kind);
    if (view.issues[act.id]) return no("an issue has this id");
    if (act.parent && !view.issues[act.parent]) return no("no such parent", true);
    const issue = facts({ id: act.id, kind: act.kind, about: act.about, state: wf.start, labels: act.labels || [], parent: act.parent, opener: caller.actor, by: {}, reviews: [] });
    return test(wf.open, issue) ? { allow: true, workflow: hash, state: wf.start } : no("the workflow's open guard refuses");
  }
  const i = view.issues[act.id];
  if (!i || i.hidden) return no("no such issue", true);
  const wf = view.workflows[i.workflow];
  if (!wf) return no("the issue's workflow is not kept");
  const issue = facts(i);
  // Fixed: whoever may not read an issue does nothing to it, and is told no more than that it is not there.
  if (act.type !== "read" && !test(wf.read, issue)) return no("no such issue", true);
  if (act.type === "move") {
    const from = wf.moves.filter((m) => m.to === act.to && (m.from === "*" || [].concat(m.from).includes(i.state)));
    if (!from.length) return no(`no move from ${i.state} to ${act.to}`);
    const m = from.find((m) => test(m.guard, issue));
    if (!m) return no(`the guard of ${from.map((m) => m.name).join(", ")} refuses`);
    const extra = i.extra.find((x) => x.move === m.name && !test(x.guard, issue));
    return extra ? no(`this issue's guard ${extra.n} on ${m.name} refuses`) : { allow: true, name: m.name };
  }
  if (act.type === "swap") {
    if (act.swap) {
      const s = wf.swaps.find((s) => s.name === act.swap);
      if (!s) return no("the workflow lists no swap " + act.swap);
      const to = { workflow: view.policy.names[s.to.workflow], state: s.to.state };
      return view.workflows[to.workflow] && test(s.guard, issue) ? { allow: true, name: s.name, to } : no(`the guard of ${s.name} refuses`);
    }
    const hash = view.policy.names[act.workflow] || act.workflow, target = view.workflows[hash];
    if (!target || !target.states.includes(act.state)) return no("no such workflow or state");
    return caller.present ? { allow: true, name: null, to: { workflow: hash, state: act.state } } : no("a swap the workflow does not list needs the owner, present");
  }
  if (act.type === "narrow" && act.remove != null) return i.extra.some((x) => x.n === act.remove) ? present() : no("no such guard", true);
  if (act.type === "narrow" && !wf.moves.some((m) => m.name === act.move)) return no("the workflow has no move " + act.move);
  return test(wf[act.type], issue) ? { allow: true } : no(`the workflow's ${act.type} guard refuses`);
}
// %%
// An allowed act as the fields of its event. The service adds seq, key, by, origin, ray, at, prev, hash and sig.
issueEvent = (view, act, verdict) => {
  const i = view.issues[act.id], base = { id: act.id, workflow: i ? i.workflow : verdict.workflow };
  const reason = act.reason || "", refs = act.refs || [];
  if (act.type === "policy") return { type: "policy", policy: act.policy, hashes: act.hashes };
  if (act.type === "open") return { type: "opened", ...base, title: act.title, body: act.body || "", kind: act.kind, about: act.about, parent: act.parent || null, labels: act.labels || [], state: verdict.state };
  if (act.type === "comment") return { type: "commented", ...base, body: act.body };
  if (act.type === "label") return { type: "labelled", ...base, add: act.add || [], remove: act.remove || [] };
  if (act.type === "review") return { type: "reviewed", ...base, verdict: act.verdict, body: act.body || "", refs };
  if (act.type === "move") return { type: "moved", ...base, move: verdict.name, from: i.state, to: act.to, reason, refs };
  if (act.type === "swap") return { type: "swapped", ...base, swap: verdict.name, from: { workflow: i.workflow, state: i.state }, to: verdict.to, reason, ...(act.policy ? { policy: act.policy } : {}) };
  return act.remove != null ? { type: "narrowed", ...base, remove: act.remove, reason } : { type: "narrowed", ...base, move: act.move, guard: act.guard, reason };
}
// %%
// Should this event have been refused, by the view before it? null, or why. What issue.verify?guards=true asks of each event.
issueReplay = (view, e) => {
  const type = { opened: "open", commented: "comment", labelled: "label", reviewed: "review", moved: "move", swapped: "swap", narrowed: "narrow", policy: "policy" }[e.type];
  if (!type) return "no such type of event";
  const act = { ...e, type, ...(e.type === "swapped" ? { workflow: e.to.workflow, state: e.to.state } : {}) };
  const i = view.issues[e.id];
  if (i && e.workflow !== i.workflow) return "judged under a workflow the issue was not on";
  const v = issueAllowed(view, e.by, act);
  if (!v.allow) return v.why;
  if (e.type === "opened" && (e.workflow !== v.workflow || e.state !== v.state)) return "opened in another workflow or state than its kind's";
  if (e.type === "moved" && (e.move !== v.name || e.from !== i.state)) return "names another move than the one allowed";
  if (e.type === "swapped" && (e.to.workflow !== v.to.workflow || e.to.state !== v.to.state)) return "lands elsewhere than the swap says";
  return null;
}
// %%
// One event against the one before it: its seq, prev, hash and signature. null, or which is wrong.
issueCheck = async (e, prev, seq, keys) => {
  const { hash, sig, ...rest } = e;
  if (e.seq !== seq) return "seq";
  if (e.prev !== prev) return "prev";
  if (hash !== (await sha256(issueCanon(rest)))) return "hash";
  return (await keys.verify(hash, sig)) ? null : "sig";
}
// %%
// A policy checked, as the act that installs it: every guard parses, every state and workflow named is there.
issuePolicyAct = async (policy) => {
  const bad = (m) => {
    throw Object.assign(new Error(m), { status: 400, code: "InvalidPolicy" });
  };
  const name = /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$/, list = (v) => Array.isArray(v) && v.every((s) => typeof s === "string" && name.test(s));
  if (!policy || typeof policy !== "object" || !policy.workflows || typeof policy.workflows !== "object" || !policy.kinds || typeof policy.kinds !== "object") bad("policy: { workflows, kinds }");
  if (JSON.stringify(policy).length > issuesLimits.policy) bad(`policy: ${issuesLimits.policy} characters at most`);
  const names = Object.keys(policy.workflows);
  if (!names.length || names.length > 20 || !names.every((n) => name.test(n))) bad("workflows: 1 to 20, named a-z 0-9 -");
  for (const n of names) {
    const w = policy.workflows[n], at = `workflow ${n}: `;
    if (!w || !list(w.states) || !w.states.length) bad(at + "states");
    if (!w.states.includes(w.start)) bad(at + "start is not one of its states");
    if (!list(w.closed) || !w.closed.every((s) => w.states.includes(s))) bad(at + "closed: a list of its states");
    if (!Array.isArray(w.moves) || !Array.isArray(w.swaps)) bad(at + "moves and swaps are lists");
    const guard = (label, g) => {
      if (typeof g !== "string" || !g || g.length > 2000) bad(at + label + " needs a guard");
      try {
        checkedRule(at + label, g);
      } catch (e) {
        bad(e.message);
      }
    };
    for (const a of ["read", "open", "comment", "label", "review", "narrow"]) guard(a, w[a]);
    for (const m of w.moves) {
      if (!m || !name.test(m.name || "")) bad(at + "a move needs a name");
      if (!(m.from === "*" || [].concat(m.from).every((s) => w.states.includes(s))) || !w.states.includes(m.to)) bad(at + `the move ${m.name} names a state it does not have`);
      guard("the move " + m.name, m.guard);
    }
    for (const s of w.swaps) {
      if (!s || !name.test(s.name || "")) bad(at + "a swap needs a name");
      const target = s.to && policy.workflows[s.to.workflow];
      if (!target || !Array.isArray(target.states) || !target.states.includes(s.to.state)) bad(at + `the swap ${s.name} names a workflow or state that is not there`);
      guard("the swap " + s.name, s.guard);
    }
  }
  for (const [k, n] of Object.entries(policy.kinds)) if (!name.test(k) || !policy.workflows[n]) bad(`kinds: ${k} names no workflow`);
  const hashes = {};
  for (const n of names) hashes[n] = await sha256(issueCanon(policy.workflows[n]));
  return { type: "policy", policy, hashes };
}
// %%
// A request's body as an act, or a 400.
issueAct = (type, b) => {
  const L = issuesLimits;
  const bad = (m) => {
    throw Object.assign(new Error(m), { status: 400, code: "InvalidRequest" });
  };
  const text = (v, max, label, need) => {
    if (v == null || v === "") return need ? bad(label) : "";
    if (typeof v !== "string" || v.length > max) bad(`${label}: text, ${max} characters at most`);
    return v;
  };
  const name = (v, label, need) => {
    const s = text(v, 60, label, need);
    if (s && !/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$/.test(s)) bad(label + ": a-z 0-9 -");
    return s;
  };
  const names = (v, label) => {
    if (v == null) return [];
    if (!Array.isArray(v) || v.length > L.labels) bad(label);
    return [...new Set(v.map((x) => name(x, label, true)))];
  };
  const refs = (v) => {
    if (v == null) return [];
    if (!Array.isArray(v) || v.length > L.refs) bad("refs");
    return v.map((r) => ({ kind: name(r && r.kind, "refs.kind", true), value: text(r && r.value, 500, "refs.value", true) }));
  };
  b = b && typeof b === "object" ? b : {};
  const id = name(b.id, "id", type !== "open"), reason = text(b.reason, L.reason, "reason");
  if (id.length > 40) bad("id: 40 characters at most");
  if (type === "open") {
    if (/^i\d+$/.test(id)) bad("id: i<number> is the service's to give");
    return { type, ...(id ? { id } : {}), title: text(b.title, L.title, "title", true), body: text(b.body, L.body, "body"), kind: name(b.kind, "kind", true), about: name(b.about ?? "brain", "about", true), parent: name(b.parent, "parent") || null, labels: names(b.labels, "labels") };
  }
  if (type === "comment") return { type, id, body: text(b.body, L.body, "body", true) };
  if (type === "label") {
    const add = names(b.add, "add"), remove = names(b.remove, "remove");
    return add.length + remove.length ? { type, id, add, remove } : bad("add or remove");
  }
  if (type === "review") return { type, id, verdict: L.verdicts.includes(b.verdict) ? b.verdict : bad("verdict: " + L.verdicts.join(", ")), body: text(b.body, L.body, "body"), refs: refs(b.refs) };
  if (type === "move") return { type, id, to: name(b.to, "to", true), reason, refs: refs(b.refs) };
  if (type === "swap") return b.swap ? { type, id, swap: name(b.swap, "swap", true), reason } : { type, id, workflow: text(b.workflow, 64, "workflow", true), state: name(b.state, "state", true), reason };
  if (b.remove != null) return Number.isInteger(b.remove) ? { type, id, remove: b.remove, reason } : bad("remove: the number of a guard");
  const guard = text(b.guard, 2000, "guard", true);
  try {
    checkedRule("guard", guard);
  } catch (e) {
    bad(e.message);
  }
  return { type, id, move: name(b.move, "move", true), guard, reason };
}
// %%
issuesApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.issue.", S = issuesSql, L = issuesLimits, J = JSON.parse;
  const refuse = (status, code, message) => Object.assign(new Error(message), { status, code });
  let made = null, keys = null;
  const schema = () =>
    (made ||= (async () => {
      for (const s of issuesSchema) await sql.exec(s);
    })().catch((e) => {
      made = null;
      throw e;
    }));
  const signer = async () => {
    if (keys) return keys;
    const text = await secrets.ISSUES_SIGNING_KEY;
    if (!text) throw refuse(503, "NotConfigured", "the secret ISSUES_SIGNING_KEY is not set");
    return (keys = await issueKeys(text));
  };
  // Who the core says is calling, and who started the chain: copied into the event, since a log line lasts 7 days.
  // How long the page waits between polls: the setting syncMs, changed with config.set and no deploy.
  const wait = () => Math.max(1000, Number(config.syncMs ?? 5000) || 5000);
  const who = (c) => ({ by: callerFrom(c.req.raw.headers), origin: originFrom(c.req.raw.headers), ray: (c.req.header("x-brain-ray") || c.req.header("cf-ray") || "").slice(0, 64) });
  // The head, the policy with every workflow, and some issues, read in one transaction.
  const load = async (rows) => {
    await schema();
    const [head, meta, found] = await sql.batch([[S.head], [S.meta], rows]);
    const view = { ...issueView(), ...(head.rows[0] ? { seq: head.rows[0].seq, head: head.rows[0].hash } : {}) };
    for (const { k, v } of meta.rows) k === "policy" ? (view.policy = J(v)) : (view.workflows[k.slice(3)] = J(v));
    for (const r of found.rows) view.issues[J(r.issue).id] = J(r.issue);
    return view;
  };
  const metaRows = (view) => [[S.putMeta, "policy", JSON.stringify(view.policy)], ...Object.entries(view.workflows).map(([hash, w]) => [S.putMeta, "wf/" + hash, JSON.stringify(w)])];
  const issueRow = (i) => [S.putIssue, i.id, i.state, i.kind, i.about, i.parent, i.workflow, i.closed ? 1 : 0, i.updated_at, JSON.stringify(i)];
  // One event more. The insert is of seq = head + 1, the table's key: of two writers at one head one fails, reads the
  // head again and writes after the other. The view's row is written in the same transaction.
  const append = async (ctx, key, given) => {
    if (typeof key !== "string" || !key || key.length > L.key) throw refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", `key: text, ${L.key} characters at most`);
    const sign = await signer();
    for (let attempt = 0; ; attempt++) {
      const view = await load([S.near, given.id || "", given.parent || ""]);
      const kept = (await sql.exec(S.byKey, key)).rows[0];
      if (kept) return { event: J(kept.event), duplicate: true };
      // The default policy is written only into an empty record. A record with no policy in its view has lost the view.
      if (!view.policy && view.seq) throw refuse(503, "ViewLost", "the view has no policy: issue.rebuild makes it again from the record");
      if (!view.policy && given.type !== "policy") {
        await append({ by: { caller: "worker:brain-x-issues", via: "" }, origin: ctx.origin, ray: ctx.ray }, "policy/default", await issuePolicyAct(issuesDefaultPolicy));
        continue;
      }
      const seq = view.seq + 1, act = given.type === "open" && !given.id ? { ...given, id: "i" + seq } : given;
      const verdict = issueAllowed(view, ctx.by, act);
      if (!verdict.allow) throw refuse(verdict.missing ? 404 : 403, verdict.missing ? "NotFound" : "Refused", verdict.why);
      const e = { seq, key, ...issueEvent(view, act, verdict), by: ctx.by, origin: ctx.origin, ray: ctx.ray, at: Date.now(), prev: view.head };
      e.hash = await sha256(issueCanon(e));
      e.sig = await sign.sign(e.hash);
      issueApply(view, e);
      try {
        await sql.batch([[S.insert, seq, key, e.id || null, e.type, e.at, e.hash, JSON.stringify(e)], ...(e.type === "policy" ? metaRows(view) : [issueRow(view.issues[e.id])])]);
        return { event: e };
      } catch (err) {
        // Another writer took this seq, or this key: go round again. Anything else is an error.
        const head = (await sql.exec(S.head)).rows[0];
        if (attempt >= 5 || ((head ? head.seq : 0) < seq && !(await sql.exec(S.byKey, key)).rows[0])) throw err;
      }
    }
  };
  const run = (fn) => async (c) => {
    try {
      return c.json(await fn(c, c.req.method === "POST" ? await c.req.json().catch(() => ({})) : c.req.query()));
    } catch (e) {
      if (e && e.status) return c.json({ error: e.code, message: e.message }, e.status);
      throw e;
    }
  };
  for (const type of ["open", "comment", "label", "review", "move", "swap", "narrow"])
    app.post(NS + type, run(async (c, b) => {
      const r = await append(who(c), b && b.key, issueAct(type, b));
      return { id: r.event.id, seq: r.event.seq, ...(r.duplicate ? { duplicate: true } : {}), event: r.event };
    }));
  app.post(NS + "install", run(async (c, b) => {
    const ctx = who(c), act = await issuePolicyAct(b.policy);
    const r = await append(ctx, b.key, act), moved = [];
    for (const [old, to] of Object.entries(b.migrate && typeof b.migrate === "object" ? b.migrate : {}))
      for (const row of (await sql.exec(S.onWorkflow, old)).rows) {
        const i = J(row.issue);
        await append(ctx, `${b.key}/${i.id}`.slice(0, L.key), { type: "swap", id: i.id, workflow: String((to && to.workflow) || ""), state: ((to && to.states) || {})[i.state] || i.state, reason: "policy " + r.event.seq, policy: r.event.seq });
        moved.push(i.id);
      }
    return { seq: r.event.seq, hashes: r.event.hashes, moved, ...(r.duplicate ? { duplicate: true } : {}) };
  }));
  // What a caller is shown of an issue its workflow's read guard refuses.
  const shown = (view, by, i) => (issueAllowed(view, by, { type: "read", id: i.id }).allow ? i : { id: i.id, kind: i.kind, state: i.state, closed: i.closed, parent: i.parent, hidden: true });
  const current = (view) => (view.policy ? Object.fromEntries(Object.values(view.policy.names).map((h) => [h, view.workflows[h]])) : {});
  app.get(NS + "snapshot", run(async (c) => {
    const view = await load([S.all]), { by } = who(c);
    return { seq: view.seq, head: view.head, wait: wait(), policy: view.policy, workflows: view.workflows, issues: Object.values(view.issues).map((i) => shown(view, by, i)).map((i) => (i.closed && !i.hidden ? { ...i, body: undefined, bodyLeftOut: true } : i)) };
  }));
  app.get(NS + "sync", run(async (c, q) => {
    await schema();
    const after = Math.max(0, Number(q.after) || 0), events = (await sql.exec(S.after, after, Math.min(L.page, Math.max(1, Number(q.limit) || 200)))).rows.map((r) => J(r.event));
    const view = await load(events.length ? [S.all] : [S.near, "", ""]), { by } = who(c);
    if (after > view.seq) return { seq: view.seq, wait: wait(), reset: true, events: [] };
    const seen = (e) => e.type === "policy" || !view.issues[e.id] || !shown(view, by, view.issues[e.id]).hidden;
    return { seq: view.seq, wait: wait(), events: events.map((e) => (seen(e) ? e : { seq: e.seq, id: e.id, type: e.type, at: e.at, hidden: true, issue: shown(view, by, view.issues[e.id]) })) };
  }));
  app.get(NS + "get", run(async (c, q) => {
    const view = await load([S.near, String(q.id || ""), ""]), { by } = who(c), i = view.issues[q.id];
    if (!i) throw refuse(404, "NotFound", "no such issue");
    const issue = shown(view, by, i);
    if (issue.hidden) return { issue, children: [], events: [] };
    return { issue, children: Object.values(view.issues).filter((k) => k.parent === i.id).map((k) => shown(view, by, k)).map((k) => (k.hidden ? k : { id: k.id, title: k.title, kind: k.kind, state: k.state, closed: k.closed })), events: (await sql.exec(S.of, i.id)).rows.map((r) => J(r.event)) };
  }));
  app.get(NS + "list", run(async (c, q) => {
    const view = await load([S.all]), { by } = who(c);
    const pass = (i) => (!q.state || i.state === q.state) && (!q.kind || i.kind === q.kind) && (!q.about || i.about === q.about) && (!q.parent || i.parent === q.parent) && (!q.label || (i.labels || []).includes(q.label));
    // What a caller may not read is matched by its state, kind and parent only: a label would say what it is.
    return { issues: Object.values(view.issues).map((i) => shown(view, by, i)).filter(pass).sort((a, b) => (b.updated_at || 0) - (a.updated_at || 0)).slice(0, Math.min(L.page, Math.max(1, Number(q.limit) || 100))).map((i) => (i.hidden ? i : { ...i, body: undefined })) };
  }));
  app.get(NS + "policy", run(async (c, q) => {
    const view = await load([S.near, "", ""]);
    if (q.hash) return view.workflows[q.hash] ? { hash: q.hash, workflow: view.workflows[q.hash] } : Promise.reject(refuse(404, "NotFound", "no such workflow"));
    return { policy: view.policy, workflows: current(view) };
  }));
  app.get(NS + "key", run(async () => ({ alg: "Ed25519", key: (await signer()).public })));
  // Every event in order, a page at a time.
  const walk = async (after, each) => {
    for (;;) {
      const rows = (await sql.exec(S.after, after, L.page)).rows;
      if (!rows.length) return;
      for (const r of rows) {
        const e = J(r.event), stop = await each(e);
        if (stop) return stop;
        after = e.seq;
      }
    }
  };
  app.get(NS + "verify", run(async (c, q) => {
    await schema();
    const sign = await signer(), guards = q.guards === "true", view = issueView();
    let seq = guards ? 0 : Math.max(0, Number(q.after) || 0), prev = "", checked = 0;
    if (seq) {
      const at = (await sql.exec(S.one, seq)).rows[0];
      if (!at) throw refuse(404, "NotFound", "no event " + seq);
      prev = J(at.event).hash;
    }
    const bad = await walk(seq, async (e) => {
      const chain = await issueCheck(e, prev, seq + 1, sign);
      if (chain) return { ok: false, seq: seq + 1, why: chain, checked };
      if (guards) {
        const why = issueReplay(view, e) || (e.type === "policy" && issueCanon((await issuePolicyAct(e.policy).catch(() => ({}))).hashes) !== issueCanon(e.hashes) ? "the policy's hashes are not its workflows'" : null);
        if (why) return { ok: false, seq: e.seq, why, checked };
